 people and and  individuals who enjoy skiing and  snowboarding obviously it's not  everybody it's some people will consider  it a bit of a luxury anyway but they'll  really worry about future holidays as  well is it something that you think we  should be concerned about  i think we should be concerned about  everything that's going to be impacted  by the climate crisis and the one thing  that i am pleased about if i can phrase  it that way is that this is getting  attention and it's raising awareness to  the fact that even something like the  olympics the winter olympics and snow  sports are going to be impacted by  climate change and really i hope it  makes us look at not just snow but  actually the olympics as a whole as a  process as something that happens every  four years how we can make that more  sustainable and really raise awareness  of all the areas that are going to be  impacted by this and even if you don't  ski it's still nice to be able to go out  on a snowy day and see something that  should be natural in many places around  the world and i think this will  hopefully get us moving even quicker  towards the sustainable future that we  need so that we can enjoy skiing on the  slopes so laura do you think this whole  conversation actually is good for  raising awareness then as you're saying  i mean that the fact that people will  think  be surprised perhaps to know that  they're going to be fewer and fewer  possible locations in the future for the  winter olympics they may have to travel  further for  for a winter skiing holiday at least it  raises awareness of the issues  i think it is really important and  actually artificial snow has been used  before in winter olympics not 100 of it  but even as far back as the 1980s we  were using it to top up our winter  olympic sports and i think it's now that  we realize because our awareness has  been raised through many other things  that we are starting to pay attention  and there's been studies done in the  